gcal — Google Calendar in a local store: search it offline, find free time, change events.

Usage: gcal <profile> <command> [options]
Account commands start with your profile, a name you choose; none is ever assumed.

What you can do:
  calendars sync <calendar>                  choose calendars; only these are copied
  sync                                       copy what changed since the last sync
  search "budget review"                     every stored event, by words and meaning, offline
  events list week person:ana@example.com    this week's events with one person
  calendars busy week --duration-minutes 30  free stretches the calendars share
  events create <calendar> --title …         add an event; attendees are mailed only if you say
  --read-only …                              this run refuses every change

Works with:
  tg                                         Telegram in the same local store: search, review and tasks offline
  max                                        MAX in the same local store: search, review and tasks offline
  wa                                         WhatsApp in the same local store: search, review and tasks offline
  zm                                         Zoom meetings: transcripts and summaries, searchable with your other WireCat data
  drive                                      Google Drive and Docs as local text, searchable with your other WireCat data
  memo context <person>                      one person across messengers, mail, notes and meetings

Start here:   gcal personal session start  (any profile name works)
Next:         gcal commands                every command, by section
              gcal guide                   scenarios: command sequences for common tasks
              gcal help options            output, offline, timeouts, dry run
